## APPROACH
- For each char, branch on whether it is '(', ')', or other.
- Opening parens push their index; closing parens try to pop a match.
- An unmatched closing paren or leftover stack entries mark invalid indices.

## PSEUDOCODE
```text
for i in 0..chars.length-1:
    c = chars[i]
    if c == '(':
        stack.push(i)
    else if c == ')':
        if stack.isEmpty():
            invalid.add(i)
        else:
            stack.pop()
    // any other char: no action
while not stack.isEmpty():
    invalid.add(stack.pop())
```

## CODE
```python
def loop_body(chars, i, stack, invalid):
    c = chars[i]
    if c == '(':
        stack.append(i)
    elif c == ')':
        if stack:
            stack.pop()
        else:
            invalid.add(i)
    # non-parenthesis characters need no action
```

## COMPLEXITY
- Each character is processed once: O(n) time, O(n) extra space for stack and set.

